("h3", "10.2.4 Gas exchange: stomata (Activity 10.6)"),
("p", "A thin peel from the lower surface of a leaf (rhoeo, money plant, hibiscus etc.) examined under a microscope shows tiny pores called **stomata**. Stomata on leaf surfaces allow the exchange of gases (carbon dioxide in, oxygen out in photosynthesis; the reverse in respiration)."),
("h2", "10.3 Transport in Plants"),
("h3", "10.3.1 Transport of water and minerals (Activity 10.7)"),
